      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca5ca260_e25d2c74",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 614,
      "author": {
        "id": 1107893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-11T00:36:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the old version, if otherSpecifier is null, nothing happens. In this version, if  otherSpecifier is null, we always set mNetworkSpecifier to null.\n\nAm I reading this correctly ? Is this WAI ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 614,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 614,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "a743427896d0877aacedb34ac4927691c56768db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "405ef2ac_fdec4bd5",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 614,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-11T04:08:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In practice I think this doesn\u0027t matter because this code has only one caller (NetworkRequest.Builder#setCapabilities) and in that codepath mNetworkSpecifier is guaranteed to be null. Given that there is no backwards-compatibility issue here, do you have strong feelings on which of the two behaviours this method should exhibit?",
      "parentUuid": "ca5ca260_e25d2c74",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 614,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 614,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "a743427896d0877aacedb34ac4927691c56768db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c6a80d97_a00a1c25",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 614,
      "author": {
        "id": 1107893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-11T05:07:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No not at all. I just wanted to point out this andbe sure it was a known difference.",
      "parentUuid": "405ef2ac_fdec4bd5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 614,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 614,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "a743427896d0877aacedb34ac4927691c56768db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58c59928_66041527",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 619,
      "author": {
        "id": 1107893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-11T00:36:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since is satisfiedBy is not symmetric and now that we have a class, we could think putting a reverse satifies(NetworkSpecifier other) method that would return true on any input for MatchAllNetworkSpecifier.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 619,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 619,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "a743427896d0877aacedb34ac4927691c56768db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "023f6ffe_90c39789",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 619,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-11T04:08:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would definitely allow us to remove the special-casing of MatchAllNetworkSpecifier. I\u0027m not sure if there are any other use cases, though. Perhaps it could be used in NetworkFactories as a filter to decide which specifiers to accept and which to reject?",
      "parentUuid": "58c59928_66041527",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 619,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 619,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "a743427896d0877aacedb34ac4927691c56768db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3bb1e05d_0164611f",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 619,
      "author": {
        "id": 1107893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-11T05:07:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since there is no implications to the public api, we can let this in and see which direction to take it to after a few follow-up patches involving specifiers.\n\nPersonally I don\u0027t like that there is a satisfiedBy function on the base class but that we still need a satisfiedBy-like function here too.",
      "parentUuid": "023f6ffe_90c39789",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 619,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 619,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "a743427896d0877aacedb34ac4927691c56768db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d9324854_18b12d7b",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NetworkRequest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 268,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-06T02:02:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it guaranteed that when passing null, this function will not call itself? Otherwise we could end up with a stack overflow. Might be safer to explicitly pass in \"(NetworkSpecifier) null\".",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 268,
        "startChar": 77,
        "endLine": 268,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "a743427896d0877aacedb34ac4927691c56768db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df9029b7_887fd0a8",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NetworkRequest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 268,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-06T03:26:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is guaranteed. https://docs.oracle.com/javase/specs/jls/se7/html/jls-15.html#jls-15.25\n\n15.25. Conditional Operator ? :\n...\nIf one of the second and third operands is of the null type and the type of the other is a reference type, then the type of the conditional expression is that reference type.\n...",
      "parentUuid": "d9324854_18b12d7b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 268,
        "startChar": 77,
        "endLine": 268,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "a743427896d0877aacedb34ac4927691c56768db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aaeec062_8bb2ad59",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NetworkRequest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 268,
      "author": {
        "id": 1107893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-11T00:36:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no recursive call here.\n\nThe ? operator necessarily has a well defined return type T, which can at worst be Object, but as Etan pointed out is StringNetworkSpecifier in this case.\n\nWhich means that the inner call to setNetworkSpecifier could be either on a well known T that is not String, or on Object.\n\nIf Object, then neither setNetworkSpecifier(String) nor setNetworkSpecifier(NetworkSpecifier) would match and the compiler would complain.",
      "parentUuid": "df9029b7_887fd0a8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 268,
        "startChar": 77,
        "endLine": 268,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "a743427896d0877aacedb34ac4927691c56768db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
